meta {
  name: Open the share link
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exam/{{shareToken}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.is_open: eq true
}

docs {
  The preview a share link shows before somebody commits to sitting: the paper's name,
  its shape, whether it is open.

  Deliberately thin. No questions, no author identity, no results — a preview that leaked
  a stem is a preview somebody screenshots and studies.

  Note the header: this and everything below run as the **second** user. The link is the
  whole access grant — no roster, no invitation — but the caller still has to be signed
  in, because a result has to belong to somebody in order to come back to the author.

  Resolved by a SECURITY DEFINER function rather than a policy, because a prospective
  sitter cannot see the row that starting would let them see: see the code, join the
  room; join the room, see the code.
}
